
==============================================================================
Lane berggren_edge_transport: Berggren children of Collatz-family edges
==============================================================================

### S1  PROVED: Berggren children in root coordinates (s,t)=(m+n,m-n)
  B1: Euclid (m,n)->(2*m - n, m)  ==  roots (s,t)->(3*m - n, m - n)
  B2: Euclid (m,n)->(2*m + n, m)  ==  roots (s,t)->(3*m + n, m + n)
  B3: Euclid (m,n)->(m + 2*n, n)  ==  roots (s,t)->(m + 3*n, m + n)
  matrices on (s,t): B1=[[1,2],[0,1]] det 1, B2=[[2,1],[1,0]] det -1, B3=[[2,-1],[1,0]] det 1
  numeric check on all primitive Euclid pairs m<=60: 2211 children agree, all odd coprime s>t>=1
  (THM-3756 (25): L=B1, M=B2, R=B3 on the odd roots (q,d)=(2r-1,2s-1); CITED, not re-proved)

### S2  PROVED: transport table (a,b,k) -> child edge, symbolic identity in x
  case A (y>x): s=y,t=x
    B1: child ((2*K*x + a*x + b)/K, x) ; edge x -> u=(2*K*x + a*x + b)/K ; family (a',b',k')=(2*K + a, b, k)  [x-type]
    B2: child ((K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K, (a*x + b)/K) ; edge u=(K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K -> y with  a*u + b = (K + 2*a)*y   [y-type; E-edge (a,b,log2 M) iff M is a power of two]
    B3: child ((-K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K, (a*x + b)/K) ; edge u=(-K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K -> y with  a*u - b = (-K + 2*a)*y   [y-type; E-edge (a,-b,log2 M) iff M is a power of two]
  case B (y<x): s=x,t=y
    B1: child ((K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K, (a*x + b)/K) ; edge u=(K*x + 2*a*x + 2*b)/K -> y with  a*u + b = (K + 2*a)*y   [y-type; E-edge (a,b,log2 M) iff M is a power of two]
    B2: child ((2*K*x + a*x + b)/K, x) ; edge x -> u=(2*K*x + a*x + b)/K ; family (a',b',k')=(2*K + a, b, k)  [x-type]
    B3: child ((2*K*x - a*x - b)/K, x) ; edge x -> u=(2*K*x - a*x - b)/K ; family (a',b',k')=(2*K - a, -b, k)  [x-type]
  Both cases give the same three unordered child pairs {x,y+2x},{x+2y,y},{2y-x or 2x-y, y or x};
  x-type children keep the SOURCE x and shift the multiplier by +-2^(k+1); y-type children keep
  the TARGET y and the multiplier a, and are E-edges iff M = +-2^k + 2a is a positive power of two.
  numeric transport identities verified on 20233 edges (a<=15 odd, |b|<=15 odd, x<400): all pass

  lead's table for a=3, b=1, k=1 (x=3,7,...,31), children in root coordinates:
       x      y |        B1 pair family                 |        B2 pair family                 |        B3 pair family                
       3      5 |        (11, 3) x->11 in (7,1,1)       |        (13, 5) 13->5 in (3,1,3)       |         (7, 5) 7->5 in (3,-1,2)      
       7     11 |        (25, 7) x->25 in (7,1,1)       |       (29, 11) 29->11 in (3,1,3)      |       (15, 11) 15->11 in (3,-1,2)    
      11     17 |       (39, 11) x->39 in (7,1,1)       |       (45, 17) 45->17 in (3,1,3)      |       (23, 17) 23->17 in (3,-1,2)    
      15     23 |       (53, 15) x->53 in (7,1,1)       |       (61, 23) 61->23 in (3,1,3)      |       (31, 23) 31->23 in (3,-1,2)    
      19     29 |       (67, 19) x->67 in (7,1,1)       |       (77, 29) 77->29 in (3,1,3)      |       (39, 29) 39->29 in (3,-1,2)    
      23     35 |       (81, 23) x->81 in (7,1,1)       |       (93, 35) 93->35 in (3,1,3)      |       (47, 35) 47->35 in (3,-1,2)    
